## 2: Calculate the adjugate (adjoint) of the matrix
The adjugate of the matrix is $\left(
\begin{array}{cc}
-3 & \frac{1}{2} \\
-\frac{7}{2} & -2 \\
\end{array}
\right)$.

## 3: Calculate the inverse of the matrix
The inverse of the matrix $A$ is given by $A^{-1} = \frac{1}{det(A)} \times adj(A)$. So, $A^{-1} = \frac{4}{31} \times \left(
\begin{array}{cc}
-3 & \frac{1}{2} \\
-\frac{7}{2} & -2 \\
\end{array}
\right) = \left(
\begin{array}{cc}
\frac{-3 \times 4}{31} & \frac{1}{2} \times \frac{4}{31} \\
\frac{-7}{2} \times \frac{4}{31} & \frac{-2 \times 4}{31} \\
\end{array}
\right) = \left(
\begin{array}{cc}
\frac{-12}{31} & \frac{2}{31} \\
\frac{-14}{31} & \frac{-8}{31} \\
\end{array}
\right)$.

